# Code of Conduct

## Our Pledge

We pledge to make participation in this project a welcoming and respectful
experience for everyone, regardless of background, identity, experience,
or level of technical knowledge.

## Our Standards

Examples of positive behavior include:

- Being respectful and considerate.
- Welcoming different viewpoints and experiences.
- Giving constructive feedback.
- Focusing on what is best for the project and community.

Unacceptable behavior includes harassment, discrimination, personal attacks,
and other conduct that creates an unsafe or hostile environment.

## Enforcement Responsibilities

Project maintainers are responsible for clarifying and enforcing the standards
of acceptable behavior and may take appropriate corrective action.

## Scope

This Code of Conduct applies to project spaces, repositories, discussions,
issues, pull requests, and other interactions related to the project.

## Enforcement

Instances of unacceptable behavior may be reported to the project maintainers.
All reports will be reviewed fairly and handled appropriately.

## Enforcement Guidelines

Maintainers may take actions including warnings, removal of inappropriate
content, temporary restrictions, or permanent removal from project spaces,
depending on the severity of the violation.

## Attribution

This Code of Conduct is inspired by commonly used open-source community
standards, including the Contributor Covenant.
